<<~ ahu #/inscription>>
! Art Sigils — Example Zero Inscription

The following source alone carries the portable inscription. Copy both the native TW5 definition and its call, with the blank separator; exclude this meme wrapper. The entire transmitted source occupies **1019 characters**, including its line breaks; a 1,024-character ceiling serves as a portability *target*, not an ideal length.

```tiddlywiki
\procedure art(worktype:"artwork" subject read imagery:"follow subject and read" treatment:"suit the read" composition:"serve the read" relation:"where meaningful" depiction-scope:"follow worktype and imagery") <<worktype>>: <<subject>>. Read: <<read>>. Imagery: <<imagery>>. Treatment: <<treatment>>. Composition: <<composition>>. Relation: <<relation>>. Depiction scope: <<depiction-scope>>.

<<art worktype=`concept-art pinboard` subject=`shattered Olympos, Rift of Tempes, Phlegra` read=`painted high pass fails a terrain check` imagery=`plan-oblique fantasy terrain with green-ochre-snow hypsometric tints; vellum route; charcoal relic; green refuge` treatment=`Tom Patterson and Bernhard Jenny shaded relief; Heinrich Berann panorama; Luka Rejec mythpunk; Piranesi/Ian Miller Phlegra charcoal; varied papers` composition=`sunlit watercolor map over uneven pinned studies` relation=`red path ends at cliff; white route takes lower saddle; bone or machine?` depiction-scope=`board fills frame; figures in studies`>>
```
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/literal-rendering>>
!! Literal rendering — Inscription null test

This ahu supplies a **hand-derived literal expansion** of the native TW5 single-line procedure. It serves as a test oracle, not a claim that this assistant ran TW5. Paste the procedure declaration and invocation together into a live TiddlyWiki5 v5.4.0+ instance; compare the rendered textual content, allowing for browser whitespace normalization and surrounding tiddler layout. Copy the characters inside the text block, not the enclosing code fences.

!!! A. Explicit Example Zero call — expected output

```text
concept-art pinboard: shattered Olympos, Rift of Tempes, Phlegra. Read: painted high pass fails a terrain check. Imagery: plan-oblique fantasy terrain with green-ochre-snow hypsometric tints; vellum route; charcoal relic; green refuge. Treatment: Tom Patterson and Bernhard Jenny shaded relief; Heinrich Berann panorama; Luka Rejec mythpunk; Piranesi/Ian Miller Phlegra charcoal; varied papers. Composition: sunlit watercolor map over uneven pinned studies. Relation: red path ends at cliff; white route takes lower saddle; bone or machine?. Depiction scope: board fills frame; figures in studies.
```

All eight arguments in the Example Zero call carry explicit values. TW5 should therefore never need a default for this case. The `<<...>>` tokens in the definition substitute their matching named call values in textual order; the procedure's period-and-space separators remain literal.

!!! B. Delegated defaults — expected output

```tiddlywiki
<<art subject=`a distant coast` read=`the unseen seems near`>>
```

```text
artwork: a distant coast. Read: the unseen seems near. Imagery: follow subject and read. Treatment: suit the read. Composition: serve the read. Relation: where meaningful. Depiction scope: follow worktype and imagery.
```

This second probe omits `worktype`, `imagery`, `treatment`, `composition`, `relation` and `depiction-scope`, making the colon/double-quote **declaration** defaults visible in the rendered result. The `=` plus backtick **invocation** values remain plain text, not required printed inscriptions.

!!! C. Null-test boundaries

* The Inscription budget counts definition, two newline separators and invocation only: **1019 characters**. This ahu lives outside that transmitted source.
* Rendering checks literal substitution, parameter order, defaults, and punctuation; it does not test whether a text-to-image model follows the compositional direction.
* Any deliberate backtick payload containing actual double-quote characters should render those characters verbatim. Avoid output-text quotations when testing Midjourney unless visible text belongs to the intended work.
* A failed comparison could indicate TW5 version, definition scope, code-fence copying, unresolved procedure registration, or different whitespace normalization; do not immediately infer a semantic failure of the Art Sigil language.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bounds>>
!! Reading, cartographic illusion, and competing papers

* **Upper image.** The main painting asks for a plan-oblique fantasy terrain view, with green lowlands, ochre middle elevations, pale snowy heights and plausible connected relief. Hypsometric tints describe a representational method, not real surveyed elevation classes or immutable Elyncian geography. A sunlit watercolor map should remain the dominant artwork.
* **The dispute.** The apparently traversable painted high pass fails a terrain check: a red line stops at a cliff; a revised white route takes a lower saddle. The actual geometry should carry that argument before a caption explains it. The dark relic invites incompatible bone and machine readings; an inhabited green refuge offers a counter-narrative to total desolation.
* **Artist-bearing roles.** Tom Patterson and Bernhard Jenny remain a paired shaded-relief reference. Heinrich Berann now directly supports the panoramic oblique view. Luka Rejec contributes exploratory mythpunk; Piranesi and Ian Miller stay localized to dark Phlegra charcoal, not the luminous landscape. Distinct papers, vellum and painting supports matter beyond differences of hue.
* **Outer scope.** Only the pinned artboard occupies the outer frame, not an art studio, diorama or in-world shrine. Figures may appear in subordinate studies. The artist names, real-world Olympus references, title text and source photos guide artistic decisions but do not require printed credits or labels.
* **Compression boundary.** The standalone source prioritizes the central plan-oblique and hypsometric landscape, with route correction, unresolved relic and refuge pinned around it. The expanded Folio carries competing historical hypotheses, hazard-color swatches and material investigations; an Inscription need not represent every study within the portability ceiling.
* **Native TW5 contract.** The generic `art()` declaration remains byte-identical to the procedures meme: colon plus double-quoted defaults in the definition, equals plus backtick-wrapped values in the call. An image receiver may treat text-like syntax as pictorial content rather than executing TW5. The expected prose under the literal-rendering ahu follows exact substitution, not an assumed execution inside Midjourney.
* **Research handoff.** The real Olympus relief, aerial and embodied-photo URIs remain external in the Folio. The operator controls aspect ratio and engine settings outside the Inscription; the transmitted source carries no engine-specific aspect or style flag.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/aftermath>>
!! Aftermath — portable witness and revision boundary

Preserve the 1,019-character native source and its literal prose oracle together when comparing artistic interpretations. The prose expansion checks text substitution; neither form guarantees a generated image will depict the same spatial or narrative relations. Record different receivers' observations and the operator's selected variants outside the transmitted source.

A productive deviation may prompt an expressly revised Inscription or a more detailed Folio. Until then, the visible artboard's failed route, disputed relic and inhabited refuge retain their authored functions without becoming verified geographic, archaeological or setting facts. Example Zero's artists, sites, paper choices and subject remain local to this worked artwork; they set no defaults for the generic Art Sigils procedures.
<<~/ahu>>
